{
  "_comment": "On the saas branch there is deliberately NO 'default' project: a bare `firebase deploy` must fail with 'No currently active project' rather than reach the live Kiryat Ono app. Deploy explicitly — `--project saas` for the multi-club version, `--project prod` only when you really mean the live one. The main branch keeps default=prod for Kiryat Ono hotfixes.",
  "_why_absent_not_placeholder": "This used to be default=UNSET-PASS-PROJECT-EXPLICITLY. That blocked deploys, but an invalid project id fails the CLI at STARTUP, so it also broke `firebase login` — a command that needs no project at all — with a confusing 'Invalid project id' before it did anything. Omitting the key blocks exactly what should be blocked and nothing else.",
  "projects": {
    "prod": "basketball-schedule-f0f57",
    "saas": "basketball-all"
  }
}
